course: dictionary
lesson: 15546
title: Extra words: superfluous
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Superfluous means more than is needed. It means extra and not necessary. Think of a bag packed with things you will never use: those things are superfluous.
explain: «Cut the superfluous words from your sentence.» The writer does not need those extra words. Once they are removed, the sentence still says everything it needs to say.
explain: Superfluous can also mean not wanted or useful, as in «Tom felt superfluous when the team had enough players.» Tom was not needed. To check, swap in a simpler word like extra or unnecessary and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Superfluous means more than is needed, extra and not necessary.
fact: Superfluous is a formal word, so you will often meet it in exam questions.
fact: In writing, superfluous words and repeated words can be cut to make your work clearer.
fact: In maths, some information in a problem may be superfluous: you do not need it to solve the problem.
fact: Useful phrases are «superfluous detail», «superfluous information» and «feel superfluous».
exercise: «Cut the superfluous words from your sentence.» What does superfluous mean here? | Long and beautiful | Written in ink | Very important and needed | *Extra and not needed
exercise: «Sam has 4 apples and 3 pears. The bag is blue.» In this maths question, why might the colour of the bag be superfluous? | *Because you do not need it to solve the problem | Because bags are always superfluous | Because blue is the best colour | Because the colour is the answer to the question
exercise: «Tom felt superfluous when the team had enough players.» What does superfluous suggest? | Very tired | Lucky | Very good at football | *Not needed or not wanted
test: «The story was clear, though it had superfluous detail about the weather.» What does superfluous detail mean? | Detail written in red | *Extra detail that is not needed | A map of the town | Detail that is very helpful
test: Which word could replace superfluous in «Remove any superfluous words» and keep the same meaning? | *Unnecessary | Loud | Helpful | Long
exam: Which sentence uses superfluous correctly? | I ran superfluous to the bus stop. | Superfluous is a colour of paint. | *The editor cut the superfluous words, because the sentence was clear without them. | The cake was superfluous, so we ate it all.
